        "text": "Since there's no entity acting as a custodian, some consider decentralized exchanges a better choice than centralized exchanges. Another upside is that most decentralized exchanges don't require you to provide any personal information other than a blockchain wallet address offering a higher degree of privacy. But using decentralized exchanges requires taking custody of your own funds and usually a decent amount of technical expertise. You're also entirely responsible for all your funds and actions. While you can call customer service when you run into any problems when using a good centralized exchange, there is zero customer support when using decentralized exchanges. For those who are new to crypto, it's generally considered preferable to begin the crypto journey with a reputable centralized exchange. As you gain more experience and expertise, you should explore a wide range of centralized and decentralized exchanges to find the exchanges that best suit your needs.",
